course: dictionary
lesson: 7427
title: Political: about power and people
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Political» is about how a country is run and who holds the power. When you meet it, ask: is this about government, voting or leaders? The context gives clues. «A political party is like a team built around ideas» tells you the word is about groups that want to lead.
explain: «Political» can also describe power and arguments inside a smaller group, such as a school or a company. Words can have more than one meaning, so use the clues to choose the right one.
explain: Check a word by swapping in your meaning. «People who love each other can still vote differently, and big holidays often bring political arguments to the table.» If you swap in "arguments about how a country should be run", the sentence still makes sense, so you have found the meaning.
fact: «Political» means about government, how a country is run and the people in power.
fact: A «political party» is a team of people who share ideas, choose candidates and try to win elections.
fact: A «manifesto» is a party's written plan of promises.
fact: A «political map» shows countries and borders, not mountains or rivers.
fact: «Political cartoons» make a point about the news with drawings, and leaders are often drawn as animals.
exercise: «A political party is like a team built around ideas.» What is a political party? | A type of weather | A kind of cartoon | *A team of people who share ideas and try to win elections | A map of rivers and mountains
exercise: Which kind of map shows countries and their borders, not mountains? | A weather map | *A political map | A physical map of mountains and rivers | A treasure map
exercise: «Political cartoons make a point about the news with drawings.» What is a political cartoon for? | *To make a point about the news | To sell ice cream | To teach you to swim | To show how tall the mountains are
test: «Big holidays often bring political arguments to the table.» In this sentence, political arguments are about? | Which cake to bake | *Ideas about how a country should be run | What colour the walls should be | How far away the beach is
test: Jayden says, «It's all political» means the choice was made for fairness. Is he right? | Yes, because political means about fish | *No, it means decisions are made for power, not fairness | No, it means nobody cares | Yes, because political means fair
exam: What does a manifesto usually contain? | A recipe for soup | A story about a dragon | A list of the tallest buildings | *A list of a party's promises for the future
